# Build directories. The tool is plain CMake, so out-of-source builds are the
# norm; these names cover the common conventions.
build/
build-*/
out/
cmake-build-*/

# Visual Studio drops these next to the sources when a solution is opened.
.vs/
*.vcxproj
*.vcxproj.filters
*.sln
*.user

# CMake artifacts
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
Testing/
compile_commands.json

# vcpkg manifest mode installs the dependency tree here.
vcpkg_installed/

# Python bytecode from the test scripts.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Compiled binaries and objects
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  One-off diagnostic scripts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These were written while bringing the port up on each platform and are kept
# in the working tree for future troubleshooting, but they are not part of the
# project: they hardcode paths from the machine they were used on and would rot
# in the repository. Add them back deliberately if one turns out to be worth
# keeping.

# Serial/HID transport debugging.
scripts/wsl-usb-diag.sh
scripts/wsl-hidbackend.sh
scripts/wsl-cppprobe.sh
scripts/wsl-hidprobe.sh
tests/hid_cpp_probe.cpp
tests/hid_probe.py

# A partial 8051 disassembler, written to inspect one test image.
tests/disasm8051.py

# Probed the parameter shapes of the STC manual MCP service by hand; the useful
# client is tests/stc_mcp.py, which is kept.
tests/stc_mcp_probe.py

# Per-machine helpers that only make sense on the author's setup.
scripts/wsl-artifacts.sh

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Superseded build helpers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# build-variant.cmd compiled the tool with one hand-written cl command line to
# check a change in a few seconds. It hardcoded the Visual Studio Community path,
# a scratch object directory under C:\Windows\Temp, and a copy of the source
# list that had to be kept in step by hand. The CMake presets and the VSCode
# tasks replaced it.
scripts/build-variant.cmd

# reset-cmake-preset.ps1 located the CMake preset CMake Tools had remembered by
# reading VSCode's state.vscdb. That problem is solved in the tracked
# .vscode/settings.json, which pins the generator and the cache variables so
# there is no preset to remember; the script only existed to work around the
# problem it diagnosed.
scripts/reset-cmake-preset.ps1

# CMakePresets.json described the four language / build-type combinations for
# CMake Tools. The generator and NEWISP_LANG are now declared in
# .vscode/settings.json (the status bar button) and passed explicitly by the
# tasks in .vscode/tasks.json, so nothing reads this file: keeping it in the
# tree would suggest a preset workflow that is not used.
CMakePresets.json
